    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math> be positive real numbers. Suppose <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> are adjacent sides of a parallelogram <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>u</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> be the projection vectors of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>w</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> along <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>, respectively. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>|</mo><mover><mi>u</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>|</mo><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mover><mi>v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mover><mi>w</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mfenced></math> and if the area of the parallelogram <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then which of the following statements is/are TRUE?",
    "image": null
  },
